There are $155$ poems in the whole, and we're thinking about $31$ of them.

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{31}{155}
&=\dfrac{1}{5} \cdot \dfrac{31}{31}\\\\
&=\dfrac{1}{5}
\end{align}$

There are $155$ poems in the whole, and we're thinking about $186$ of them.

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{186}{155}
&=\dfrac{6}{5} \cdot \dfrac{31}{31}\\\\
&=\dfrac{6}{5}
\end{align}$
